    "created_at": "2016-05-19T16:32:52Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-19T16:32:52Z",
    "body": "This is indeed a problem. Unfortunately we can't change how the original markup is parsed. Your proposed workaround also doesn't help in general. Consider `<table><form><tr><td><input>`. First pass the form is empty, child of the table, but the input is still associated with it. On serialize-reparse, the DOM is the same but the association is lost. There are no doubt more examples.\n\nAlso, come to think of it, foster parenting can also cause nested `p`s or nested `a`s, and I think AAA can also cause nested `a`s, which doesn't roundtrip. \n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
