    "created_at": "2016-05-19T19:40:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-19T19:40:19Z",
    "body": "Whether things work just fine is very much dependent on what the page is doing. Pages break completely for seemingly minor things.\n\nMy example doesn't do foster parenting. But also breaking form association or moving form controls in the DOM is certainly going to break pages.\n\nNote that legacy IE did usually roundtrip form association (but it didn't use a tree for the DOM), and it was a known problem that form association didn't work with innerHTML. But it was rare enough that browsers got away with breaking it.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
